                        "entry_id": "7451e317-b49a-37b4-ba5c-1d05918ae1f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being under narcosis; unconsciousness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "89966ca7-79ea-4491-8466-9172871c56b8",
                                "sense_id": "cd898202-42df-3829-97cd-131f8dd3d3d7",
                                "text": "Persons affected with an idiosyncrasy against this particular substance, and neurasthenic sufferers may easily be seized with a vomituritive tendency after the expiration of the narcose […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "74ead28c-290f-406a-a042-d18577878bc0",
                                "sense_id": "cd898202-42df-3829-97cd-131f8dd3d3d7",
                                "text": "If, then, all anæsthetists would insist upon complete anæsthesis before even the simplest operation was proceeded with, we should hear less frequently of the fatal results of “a few whiffs,” when death is not really due to the use of the anaesthetic, but to the shock consequent upon its not being pushed far enough before the narcose."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e432312b-845a-4be8-8b79-1bc756d972f6",
                                "sense_id": "cd898202-42df-3829-97cd-131f8dd3d3d7",
                                "text": "Chloroform was administered so as to obtain a relaxation of the muscles without producing a complete narcose."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
